{
 "entry": "mud_motor_specs",
 "kind": "PUBLISHED_DATA_SHEET_FIGURES",
 "publisher": "MS Directional (Mpact)",
 "title": "Motor Handbook, First Edition, April 2021, Version 2.1",
 "url": "https://patenergy.com/assets/filesystems/general/docs/Mud-Motor-Handbook.pdf",
 "fetched": "2026-10-17",
 "how": "Transcribed from the handbook's individual motor spec sheets, field by field, and read a second time independently; the two readings agreed on every figure kept here. On 2026-10-17 every sheet's flow range, rev/gal, differentials, torque and weight on bit were read a third time against the catalogue and agreed, and the two sheets missing from the first edition of this catalogue (7 in 8/9 4.3 and 8 in x 7 3/4 in 7/8 5.9) were each read twice and added. The PDF could not be fetched byte for byte from the build machine, so no file hash is given: check a figure against the maker's sheet before relying on it.",
 "notes": [
  "Max Torque is the sheet's maximum torque; the program takes it as the torque at the maximum differential and the slope between them as torque per psi of differential - an estimate, stated as one wherever it is used.",
  "The sheets print performance \"with water at operating temperature\"; the handbook derates the differential with temperature.",
  "Speed is rev/gal times the flow at no load; the handbook's printed speed ranges do not always equal that product.",
  "Where the handbook's summary table and a motor's own sheet differ (the 6 5/8 in 5/6 8.4 flow range: sheet 300-700 gpm, summary 350-700 gpm; the 5 5/8 in 7/8 12.0 differential and torque), the catalogue keeps the sheet's figure.",
  "The 8 in x 7 3/4 in 7/8 5.9 sheet prints two bit-to-bend values under three column labels; they are read as adjustable 83 and fixed standard 73, the layout of the 7 in x 7 3/4 in sheets."
 ],
